{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-unit-modulus-eigenvalue","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:unit-modulus-eigenvalue","kind":"proposition","title":"Unit-modulus eigenvalues on $V_{(2,1)}$ and the Borromean fixed point","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-borromean-markov-trace-closed-form","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hoefsmit-binding-amplitude"],"tags":["eigenvalue","unit-modulus","borromean","meson","wedderburn","standard-rep"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_eigenvalue_neg_one","text":"unit-modulus-eigenvalue.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:unit-modulus-eigenvalue\"></a><p><em>For any braid word <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code> of even length in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code>, the\neigenvalues of the standard representation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\rho_{(2,1)}(\\beta)</code>\nlie on the unit circle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|\\lambda| = 1</code>. The Borromean braid\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta_{\\mathrm{Bor}} = (\\sigma_1\\sigma_2^{-1})^3</code> has the\ndegenerate eigenvalue <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda = -1</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unit-modulus-eigenvalue.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.4.24"}
